         "1. Define object: a functional entity with a definite shape and identity.\n2. Define material: the chemical/physical matter from which an object is fabricated.\n3. One-to-many relationship: wood (material) -> chair, desk, pencil, cricket bat (objects).\n4. Many-to-one relationship: water tumbler (object) -> glass, steel, copper, plastic, terracotta (materials).\n5. Conclude objects are defined by function/form; materials by substance composition.",
