         "1. Solubility of gases: gases dissolve in cold water under atmospheric pressure.\n2. Dissolved oxygen (DO): typically 6 to 10 milligrams of O2 per litre of freshwater.\n3. Biological utilization: fish pump water across thin gill filaments, where blood absorbs dissolved O2 molecules by diffusion.\n4. Proof of dissolved air: gentle heating of a beaker of water shows tiny bubbles appearing on the inner glass walls long before the water boils (expelled dissolved air).",
