         "1. Optical behavior: light passes straight through with negligible scattering or reflection.\n2. Visual perception: objects behind the material appear crisp, with distinct outlines and true colours.\n3. Common examples: car windshield glass, spectacles lenses, clear cellophane tape, clean aquarium water.\n4. Conclude transparent materials provide unobstructed optical transmission.",
