         "1. Convenience and order: quick storage and retrieval in libraries, pharmacies, and grocery shops.\n2. Comparative study: studying one representative member of a group (e.g. metals) reveals properties shared by all members.\n3. Pattern recognition: identifying correlations (e.g. lustrous materials are usually hard conductors).\n4. Systematic taxonomy: foundation of chemistry (periodic table) and biology (species classification).",
